---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import { STATUS_VALUES } from '../content.config';
---
<BaseLayout title="How We Verify">
  <article class="article">
    <h1>How We Verify</h1>
    <div class="prose">
      <p>
        Reporting on alleged wrongdoing by public figures carries real legal and
        ethical responsibility. We follow a fixed checklist before anything is
        published.
      </p>
      <h2>Our sourcing rules</h2>
      <ol>
        <li><strong>Primary documents first.</strong> Court orders, charge sheets / FIRs, agency (CBI / ED / CAG / Lokayukta) reports, and election affidavits filed with the ECI.</li>
        <li><strong>At least one verifiable source per claim.</strong> The site will not build a report that has no sources attached.</li>
        <li><strong>Credible secondary reporting.</strong> Where we rely on news media, we prefer established outlets and link the original article.</li>
        <li><strong>No anonymous "facts".</strong> If we cannot point a reader to evidence, we either label it clearly as an unverified allegation or we leave it out.</li>
      </ol>
      <h2>How we describe legal status</h2>
      <p>Every report carries one of these status labels so an allegation is never confused with a conviction:</p>
      <ul>
        {STATUS_VALUES.map((s) => <li>{s}</li>)}
      </ul>
      <h2>Fairness</h2>
      <p>
        We seek or note the subject's response where available, and we offer a
        right of reply. We update reports when a case status changes — for
        example, if charges are dropped or a person is acquitted.
      </p>
    </div>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>
